==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/de|Türe}} {{i|becoming dated}}

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|gmh|de}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|turi|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} *''duri-'' {{m|gem-pro|*durz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*dʰwer-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰwor-||doorway, door, gate}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dhur-}}. Cognate with Middle Dutch ''[[dore]]'' (Dutch ''[[deur]]''), Old Norse ''[[dyrr]]'' (Swedish ''[[dörr]]'', Danish {{term|dør|lang=da}}). The Germanic word also existed in different stem-endings: ''*dora-'', {{m|gem-pro|*durą}} (German ''[[Tor]]'', Old English ''[[dor]]'' → English {{term|door|lang=en}}), ''*duru-'' (Old English ''[[duru]]'').

